# Frequency Modulation (FM)

Frequency modulation occurs when one signal affects the frequency of an oscillator. Depending on modulation speed and depth, FM can produce anything from gentle movement to complex, harmonically rich sounds.

## Why FM matters
FM allows one signal to shape another at a very fundamental level. It is often used to add brightness, complexity, or instability to a sound.

## Typical usage
- Slow FM for subtle motion
- Audio-rate FM for harmonic complexity
